    question: 'Can I deduct a desk I also use for personal stuff?',
    answer: '<p>If your desk is in a <strong>dedicated home office space</strong> used exclusively for work, you can generally deduct it fully, even if you occasionally check personal email there.</p><p>However, if the desk is in a shared space (living room, bedroom) that\'s not a dedicated office, you can only deduct the <strong>business-use percentage</strong>. A desk used 80% for work and 20% for personal would be 80% deductible.</p>'
  },
  {
    question: 'What if I buy furniture for multiple rooms?',
    answer: '<p>Only furniture in your dedicated home office qualifies for the home office deduction. A chair in your living room—even if you work there sometimes—typically doesn\'t qualify.</p><p>The key test: <strong>Is the space used regularly and exclusively for business?</strong> If yes, furniture in that space is deductible.</p>'
  },
