    question: 'Do I need to save the receipt forever?',
    answer: '<p>Keep receipts for <strong>at least 7 years</strong> from the purchase date (or longer for depreciated items). The IRS can audit returns up to 6 years back in some cases.</p><p>Digital records work: take a photo of the receipt and store it in cloud storage like Google Drive or a dedicated app like Expensify. Keep the original if possible, but digital copies are accepted.</p>'
